          "sourceDoi": "10.1098/rspa.2024.0259",
          "targetDoi": "10.1017/jfm.2022.1052",
          "snippet": "-Low-dimensional approximation: For a ROM a tractable number of observables are required that evolve accurately with time on a low-dimensional subspace. An excessive number of observables can lead to spurious eigenvalues which are non-physical and impede interpretability [20]. A nonlinear autoencoder provides good choice of observables, which, combined with the closure from a non-Markovian correction term enables an aggressively low-dimensional model.",
