      ],
      "isOa": true,
      "fulltextExcerpts": [
        "The Mori-Zwanzig formalism [6,7] enables a closed-form representation of the infinite-dimensional Koopman operator by providing a non-Markovian correction to its finite approximation. This effectively closes the gap between the practical implementation of the Koopman operator and its idealized form.",
        "Observing these problems, this work proposes an interpretable data-driven ROM termed Mori-Zwanzig autoencoder (MZ-AE), that exploits Mori-Zwanzig formalism and approximates the invariant Koopman subspace in the latent manifold of a nonlinear autoencoder. A non-Markovian correction is provided to the approximate Koopman operator which guides it back to the true trajectory upon deviation.",
        "Through the Mori-Zwanzig formalism, we provide a memory correction term to provide longer predictability.\n\nOrganization. In §2 we present the relevant background theory, briefly discussing model-order reduction, Koopman formalism and Mori-Zwanzig decomposition. In §3 we provide the details of the proposed MZ-AE algorithm. In §4 we describe the numerical experiments and discuss the results obtained. Finally, in §5 we provide a conclusion and a discussion on future work."
